+# Production PBR alpha blending smoke (2026-10-20)
+
+The SDL_GPU diagnostic `lancer --sdl-gpu-pbr-transparency-smoke` draws two identical front-facing triangles with the embedded production Freelancer PBR shader. Both receive the same directional light fixture and white diffuse texture. The left triangle writes opacity 1; the right writes `PBRParameters.Oc = 0.5`. The target is cleared to opaque black and uses the renderer's normal RGB blend factors (`SRC_ALPHA`, `ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA`) with standard source-over alpha factors.
+
+The readback passed on Mesa Vulkan / Intel Haswell:
+
+| Draw | Readback luma | Alpha after blend |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Opaque, left | 241 | 255 |
+| 50% opacity, right | 120 | 255 |
+
+The comparison image shows the corresponding opacities against the same black clear:
+
+![Production PBR opaque and half-opacity triangles](transparency-comparison.png)
+
+The Release build succeeded (0 errors). Runtime log: [`runtime.log.txt`](runtime.log.txt). Mesa reports incomplete Haswell Vulkan support, so this is a functional shader/blend-path check on one driver. It uses synthetic geometry and does not establish correct transparency sorting, real Freelancer material flags, additive/translucent asset parity, or visual quality in a complete game scene.
